A viral flyer is inviting people to gather at Cloud Gate and move the sculpture seven inches to the left. The advertised appointment is November 8 at the oddly specific time of 12:47 p.m.

There is one obvious complication: the Bean weighs about 110 tons.

Created by artist Anish Kapoor, the polished stainless steel landmark sits in Millennium Park and reflects the city skyline across its curved surface. Moving it is not exactly comparable to rearranging the living room.

Online discussion treats the invitation as another wonderfully absurd community joke. The circulating post does not establish that the city approved a relocation, that an organised attempt will happen, or that anything has actually moved.

For now, the confirmed attraction is the ridiculous premise.

